 "submission": {
  "summary": "P-3's decline is not water-driven but depletion with falling reservoir pressure. Its water cut has stayed at about 1% for its whole life with the choke unchanged at 55%, while its liquid rate and downhole pressure have fallen steadily (pressure down about 39% from 2016 to 2020) and it follows a clean hyperbolic decline, so the drop is the reservoir losing energy, not water taking capacity.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "P-3's water cut has stayed at about 1% from first oil through 2020-12-31, with no rise, so water is not taking the well's capacity.",
    "detail": "Field screen as of 2020-12-31: water_cut 0.01 (E2). Waterflood monthly water cut 0.01 every month 2016-02 to 2020-12 and by-year water_cut 0.01 in 2016 (1425 Sm3/d liquid), 2020 (295.44 Sm3/d) choke 55.0% unchanged (E4); production_monthly water_cut 0.01 each month (E5). WOR trend not fittable: 0 months with WOR >=1, need 12 (E4).",
